  <page_number>1</page_number>
  <running_head>EPIGRAMMATION.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>A</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Præsens qui placide pieq; seclum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Vult transmittere, vir bonusq; haberi,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Curis abstq; meris, molestiisq;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Is ante omnia maximum Iehouam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Sincere vereatur, atque amet, nec</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Non &amp; ante oculos sibi reponat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Verbi iussa salutis, exsequatur</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Gnauus officia &amp; vocationis:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Suum diligat intimoq; amore</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Proximum, pariter suas agat res:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Non sese ἀλλοτρίοις det implicatum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Vt sortem placide ferat, vel unum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Curet; diuitiis hiet ne opimis:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Aulai atq; fori pericla mille</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Et discrimina sed [?]dolus vitabit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Immittet rigidos subinde frenos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Linguæ, det labiis suis capistrum:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Γλωσσαγώγος non agat perinde,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Quod est esse velit, nihilq; malit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Esse quenq; sinat, quod est, simulq;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Sic est ille futurus idem &amp; usq;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Tum cubilia vitet inquinare,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Et thorum fugiat coinquinatum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Purum a crimine corpus, &amp; sagacem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Conseruans animum, piumq; pectus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Infami abstineat manusq; furto,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Sensus dirigat atq; cautus actus:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Non sit alterius, suis licet dum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Esse, nemine obesse, adesse cunctis:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30">
      <i>Hoc emblemata nostræ docebunt,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31">
      <i>Quod ipsum fauet aduouens Oraeus.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse printed as one continuous poem; line breaks are not kept, lines are run together with spaces. Greek words (ἀλλοτρίοις; Γλωσσαγώγος) are doubtful in detail and should be checked against the scan. "sed [?]dolus" is a doubtful reading of a damaged word. "nihilq; malit" and "quenq;" are doubtful. The word "Oraeus" is as printed. Bottom right "EX" is a second signature mark, not transcribed as text. The printed "1" at top right is the page number.</notes>
</page>
